--   Vendored from the LevyStochCalc library (https://github.com/cgarryZA/LevyStochCalc), commit 984dbf0b790031eac05d56fe5a84b65e15e1e932. `IsPoissonFiltration N ℱ` requires counts on measurable subsets of $(-\infty,t]\times E$ to be $\mathcal F_t$-measurable. It also requires, for every $s\ge0$, independence under $P$ between $\mathcal F_s$ and the sigma-algebra generated by counts on all measurable subsets of $(s,\infty)\times E$. `IsPoissonFiltration.indep` derives independence from $\mathcal F_s$ for a finite-mark-measure strip $(s,t]\times A$ when $0\le s<t$.
